1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,486
Rules state what the exchanged information must satisfy.

2
00:00:04,386 --> 00:00:07,516
A business rule is a statement in natural language.

3
00:00:07,516 --> 00:00:10,033
A constraint restricts information units.

4
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:14,882
An expression states the constraint in a rule language that software can check.

5
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:18,193
Open the use case, and click Business rules.

6
00:00:19,682 --> 00:00:20,321
Click Add.

7
00:00:20,321 --> 00:00:27,601
Name the rule Safety-critical defects, and write the statement: a defect flagged as safety-critical shall have the

8
00:00:27,601 --> 00:00:29,006
priority P1, Critical.

9
00:00:29,006 --> 00:00:29,709
Click Done.

10
00:00:31,282 --> 00:00:33,250
Now add a constraint for this rule.

11
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,850
Define it in the triage record, where the information units are.

12
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:41,163
Click Select IUs, and choose Safety-critical and Priority.

13
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:53,284
Write the constraint, using Insert IU reference to refer to information units by their id: if Safety-critical is

14
00:00:53,284 --> 00:00:56,046
true, then Priority equals P1, Critical.

15
00:00:56,946 --> 00:01:03,577
A formal expression in SHACL, SPARQL, Python or another rule language can be added with Add expression.

16
00:01:03,577 --> 00:01:04,285
Click Done.

17
00:01:05,185 --> 00:01:13,890
The catch-up file DMBCF_5f_rules_complete.idm is the finished IDM, with fourteen rules and their constraints.

18
00:01:13,890 --> 00:01:14,529
Open it.

19
00:01:15,429 --> 00:01:16,918
Click Validate.

20
00:01:16,918 --> 00:01:23,173
The IDM is checked against ISO 29481-3: no errors, no warnings.

21
00:01:24,073 --> 00:01:26,330
Finally, Save and Export.

22
00:01:26,330 --> 00:01:35,721
Export idmXML 2.0 to exchange the IDM with other tools, and an HTML document to share it with reviewers.

23
00:01:36,621 --> 00:01:39,071
This is the exported HTML document.

24
00:01:39,071 --> 00:01:46,424
You have built a complete IDM: header, use case, process map, exchange requirements, mappings, and rules.

25
00:01:46,424 --> 00:01:48,034
Thank you for watching.

